---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';import Crumbs from '../components/Crumbs.astro';
import {paidProduct,supportEmail} from '../lib/paid-product.mjs';
---
<Base title="Paid-beta terms — review draft" description="Draft account and subscription terms for Acquisition Companion Deal Lab. Legal review and owner approval are required before paid access opens." type="About" noindex>
 <Crumbs items={[{title:'Terms'}]}/><article class="narrow"><header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">Paid-beta preparation</p><h1>Deal Lab subscription terms</h1><p class="notice">Review draft: these subscription terms require legal review and owner approval before paid access opens. Subscriptions are not open.</p></header>
 <div class="prose"><h2>Free learning, optional paid practice</h2><p>Acquisition Companion is operated by The Wired Nomad LLC. The public course, Start Here, Topics, Financing, Examples, Quantitative Reference, Glossary, Sources and methodology remain free. {paidProduct.name} is an optional educational subscription. The initial paid beta is invite-only for customers in the United States. Operator approval and an explicit U.S.-customer attestation are required before Checkout. Approval alone does not grant Deal Lab access.</p>
 <h2>Recurring billing</h2><p>Launch pricing is ${paidProduct.monthlyUsd} per month or ${paidProduct.annualUsd} per year, in USD. The chosen subscription renews at that interval until canceled. Checkout will show the price, billing interval and any applicable tax before purchase. There is one product and no free AI trial.</p>
 <h2>Cancellation and payment problems</h2><p>You may cancel recurring billing at any time through Manage billing in your account. Access continues through the already-paid billing period unless applicable law requires otherwise. Unpaid, past-due, canceled or expired subscriptions may lose access; correcting a payment problem can restore access after billing state is verified. For access or cancellation help, contact <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>.</p>
 <h2>Refunds — legal review required</h2><p>Subscription fees are generally non-refundable after access has been used, except where required by applicable law. If you believe you were charged in error or have a billing problem, contact <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>. This policy does not limit mandatory consumer rights. Treatment of unused access and service outages must be finalized before launch.</p>
 <h2>Usage and availability</h2><p>Includes up to {paidProduct.monthlyRequestAllowance} AI requests per UTC calendar month, on either billing interval. Your account shows current usage and remaining requests. The allowance resets at 00:00 UTC on the first day of each month; it does not roll over. Requests that reach the model count even if a response fails. Access-denied, invalid or quota-denied requests do not consume the allowance. Service and model availability can vary.</p>
 <h2>Accounts and privacy</h2><p>Keep your sign-in email secure. Sign-in links expire after 15 minutes, work once and are bound to the browser where requested. You can sign out to end your session. Contact <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a> for account security, deletion or access problems. Account deletion does not by itself cancel recurring billing; cancellation and any legally required record retention must be handled together. Retention periods and the deletion procedure remain review items; see <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>.</p>
 <h2>Educational use</h2><p>Deal Lab helps you examine evidence, calculate and practice reasoning. AI may make mistakes. You retain responsibility for decisions; responses do not establish financing approval, investment suitability or transaction-specific legal, tax or accounting advice. Do not submit confidential, proprietary, personal or non-public deal material. There are no private CIM, financial-package or data-room uploads.</p>
 <h2>Support</h2><p>Need help with sign-in, billing, cancellations, bugs or product questions? <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>.</p></div></article>
</Base>
